        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "text": "The site gets all of its data from one external source: the Citadel game data API at `https://api.thecitadel.com`. It has no database or local data files, and no `.env` is checked in. Every page fetches from the API on the server when it renders. I sent a request to `/v1/kills` and `/v1/hulls` just now; both answered 200, with `/v1/kills` reporting build `d38e3a5…`.\n\nThere are two client modules, both under `src/lib/`.\n\n### 1. Kill data: [api.ts](src/lib/api.ts)\nThis covers kills, battles, pilots and totals. All requests go through one `get()` helper ([api.ts:17](src/lib/api.ts:17)):\n\n| Route | Function | Used by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/v1/kills` | `listKills` | home feed, pilot, ship and zone pages |\n| `/v1/kills/summary` | `killTotals`, `getGroupStats` | home totals, ship and zone stats |\n| `/v1/kills/{id}` | `getKill` | kill page (fitting, cargo, attackers) |\n| `/v1/battles`, `/v1/battles/{id}` | `listBattles`, `getBattle` | battles list and battle page |\n| `/v1/pilots/{id}` | `getPilot` | pilot page |\n| `/v1/leaderboards` | `getLeaderboards`, `filterOptions` | leaderboards, and the zone list in the filter bar |\n\n- Next's fetch cache refetches at most every 10 seconds, matching the API's own 10-second cache. Requests time out after 8 seconds.\n- A 404 returns `null`. Any other failure throws `KillboardUnavailable`, which the pages show as a \"signal lost\" state.\n- The five-minute publication delay on kills is applied by the API, not by this site.\n\n### 2. Names and art: [game-data.ts](src/lib/game-data.ts)\nThis covers the names, images and stat labels that kill cards point to by `def`, the game's asset id.\n- It reads six lists from `/v1/{items,hulls,npcs,stats,artifacts,ciphers}`.\n- Each server instance keeps one copy in memory, tied to a single game build (the API sends it in an `X-Citadel-Build` header).\n- Every 5 minutes it checks for changes with `If-None-Match`. It only switches to new lists when all six report the same build.\n- If the API is down, it keeps serving the last good copy and waits 30 seconds before trying again.\n- [art-server.ts](src/lib/art-server.ts) wraps this in `loadGameArt()`, which every page calls. [art.mjs](src/lib/art.mjs) and [tooltips.mjs](src/lib/tooltips.mjs) turn the lists into image URLs and module tooltips. The image URLs point back at the API.\n\n### What isn't from the API\n- **Ship-class icons**: `public/ship-class/*.webp` were converted once from the game's sprites, because the API doesn't serve class art yet ([art.mjs:23](src/lib/art.mjs:23)). Fonts and wordmarks are also local.\n- **Missing items**: if an item isn't in the current build, the site draws an SVG tile with the item's name instead (`placeholder()` in [art.mjs](src/lib/art.mjs)).\n- **Kill cam and clip links**: these arrive as URLs inside each kill (`links.killCam`, `links.clip`) and point to wherever the API says. The site opens or downloads them; it doesn't fetch them itself ([embeds.tsx](src/app/_components/embeds.tsx)).\n\n### Configuration\n- `GAME_DATA_API_URL` points the site at a different API. The default is production.\n- `GAME_DATA_API_CONTACT` sets the contact address in the `User-Agent` header the API asks for. The default is `https://thecitadel.com/killboard` ([game-data.ts:89-96](src/lib/game-data.ts:89)).\n\nThe type definitions in `api.ts` cite `tools/game-data-api/openapi/openapi.json`. That file lives in the original monorepo, not here, so this repo has nothing to check those types against.",
