        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "text": "Yes. All the game data should come from the API, and only presentation should live in the site. Most of that platform already exists: `api.thecitadel.com/v1/openapi.json` documents 37 routes, including a live kill stream (`/v1/kills/stream`), a full download (`sde.zip`), fit tools and a tooltip route (`POST /v1/items/facts`). It also allows browser requests from any site and spells out rate limits, a versioning promise and terms. This killboard just doesn't show it, because it only uses a few of those routes.\n\nA good test is whether someone who has never seen the Unity project could build this killboard from the public API alone. Today they couldn't quite, because the site still hardcodes some game knowledge. Each item below is a gap an outside developer would run into:\n\n| Game knowledge in the site | Where | What the API should serve |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Zone list.** There is no `/v1/zones`, so the filter bar takes its zones from the all-time leaderboard. A zone where nobody died never appears. | `filterOptions` in [api.ts:289](src/lib/api.ts:289) | `/v1/zones`. Kills already include `zone.id`, so the data exists. |\n| **Death causes and ship classes** are typed into the code. | `CLASSES`, `CAUSES` in [api.ts:278](src/lib/api.ts:278) | A list of the values each filter accepts. The spec only gives examples. |\n| **Which image to show.** Kill items only carry an id, so the site downloads six lists and copies the game's own image-picking rule (rarity version, else base image; artifacts fall back to their item). | [art.mjs:81](src/lib/art.mjs:81) | The image URL on each item, hull and cipher in the kill response. |\n| **The Advanced → Augmented rarity rename.** Old kills still say Advanced. | [art.mjs:9](src/lib/art.mjs:9) | Current rarity names in every response. |\n| **Tooltip wording.** The site reimplements the game's modifier text and number formatting. | [tooltips.mjs](src/lib/tooltips.mjs) | The tooltip rows on each kill item. `/v1/items/